.TH PATH_CANONICALIZE 3
.SH NAME
path_canonicalize \- convert path to canonical form
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "path.h"
.PP
.B int path_canonicalize(const char* path, stralloc* sa, int symbolic);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B path_canonicalize
processes a path string and appends the canonical version to the 
.B stralloc 
buffer 
.I sa.
It resolves '.' and '..' components.
.PP
If 
.I symbolic
is non-zero, it resolves symbolic links encountered in the path.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a value greater than 0 on success, representing the number of symlinks processed + 1. Returns 0 on error.